From a373dcf20f7620cf46d97950a68593448a5819f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:30:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Build-depend on systemd-dev, so the systemd user unit is
 installed again

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 debian/changelog | 11 +++++++++++
 debian/control   |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index 0809b46..d7c3ef8 100644
--- a/debian/changelog
+++ b/debian/changelog
@@ -1,3 +1,14 @@
+indicator-bluetooth (0.0.6+17.10.20170605-0ubuntu7+unity1) resolute; urgency=medium
+
+  * Build-depend on systemd-dev instead of systemd. systemd.pc moved to
+    systemd-dev, so configure found no systemduserunitdir and the 26.04
+    rebuild dropped /usr/lib/systemd/user/indicator-bluetooth.service;
+    without it the indicator service never starts in a systemd user
+    session.
+    (LP: #2153375)
+
+ -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0000
+
 indicator-bluetooth (0.0.6+17.10.20170605-0ubuntu7) resolute; urgency=medium
 
   * Depend on gnome-bluetooth-sendto instead of transitional package
diff --git a/debian/control b/debian/control
index 3b45aae..14cb2fc 100644
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 9.0),
                dh-translations,
                gnome-common,
                libglib2.0-dev,
-               systemd,
+               systemd-dev,
                valac (>=0.18),
 Standards-Version: 3.9.4
 Homepage: https://launchpad.net/indicator-bluetooth
-- 
2.53.0

